sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/assets/20261013T194318-162-mbmi/api_graphrag_subgraph_empty.json)\n   - Observed Schema: `{ \"nodes\": [], \"edges\": [], \"active_node_pks\": [], \"active_edge_keys\": [], \"retrieval_ms\": 0.0 }`\n\n---\n\n## 4. Explicit Deficiency Register\n\n1. **`DEF-009-01` (Stale `d3.zoom` Closure \u0026 `useEffect` Ordering Race Overwriting Canvas Illumination During Camera Transition):** In [`GraphCanvas.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/components/GraphCanvas.tsx#L76-L81), the camera framing `useEffect` (lines 77–81) runs **before** the `d3.zoom` initialization `useEffect` (lines 358–380) during the React commit phase. Consequently, `frameActiveSubgraph` starts a 350ms D3 transition on the **previous** `zoomBehaviorRef.current` instance, whose `'zoom'` listener closes over the **stale** `render` callback (`isIlluminated = false`, `activeNodePKs = Set(0)`). Once the force simulation has settled (`alpha \u003c alphaMin`), every animation frame of the 350ms camera transition (including the final frame) repaints the canvas using the stale unilluminated closure, leaving the canvas dark until a manual user gesture triggers the newly bound DOM zoom handler.\n2. **`DEF-009-02` (Re-Initialization of `d3.zoom` \u0026 Canvas Bitmap Buffer Reset on Every State/Hover Change):** In [`GraphCanvas.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/components/GraphCanvas.tsx#L358-L380), the zoom setup effect depends on `[render]`, re-creating `d3.zoom()`, re-binding DOM listeners, and resetting `canvas.width` / `canvas.height` on every state or hover change rather than separating canvas buffer sizing/zoom initialization from reactive redraws.\n3. **`DEF-009-03` (Active Node Fill Color \u0026 Radial Glow Halo Styling):** In [`GraphCanvas.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/components/GraphCanvas.tsx#L225-L240), base node fill is set unconditionally to `visual.badgeColor` (line 239) instead of rendering active nodes (`activeNodePKs`) in gold/amber (`#ffb703`) with active radial glow halos (`rgba(255, 183, 3, 0.45)`) per Requirement 4.1.3, and does not separate active radial glow halos from `selectedNode`'s persistent selection ring/pulse effect per Requirement 4.4.1.\n4. **`DEF-009-04` (De-Illumination on Closing Chat Inquiry):** In [`AgentChatDrawer.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/components/AgentChatDrawer.tsx#L71-L82) and [`GraphSyncContext.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/context/GraphSyncContext.tsx#L201), closing the chat inquiry drawer (`setIsChatOpen(false)`) does not revert `isIlluminated` to `false` or trigger `clearIllumination()` per Requirement 4.3.1.\n5. **`DEF-009-05` (Empty Subgraph Response Handling):** In [`GraphSyncContext.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/context/GraphSyncContext.tsx#L269-L273), `setIlluminatedPath` unconditionally sets `isIlluminated = true` even when `response.active_node_pks` is empty (`length === 0`), dimming the entire canvas instead of clearing illumination and maintaining baseline rendering per Section 5.3.\n6. **`DEF-009-06` (Rapid Successive Queries Handling):** In [`GraphSyncContext.tsx`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/frontend/src/context/GraphSyncContext.tsx#L340-L399), `submitInquiry` drops overlapping requests when `isQueryLoading` is true (`if (!q || isQueryLoading) return;`) rather than allowing rapid successive queries to supersede/overwrite the active path upon arrival per Section 5.1.\n7. **`DEF-009-07` (Single-Entity General Traversal Edge Key Serialization):** In [`src/graphrag/traversal.py`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/src/graphrag/traversal.py#L365-L384), `_execute_single_general_traversal` calls `.data()` on the Neo4j result (turning `r` into a tuple) and calls `_convert_edge(r, src_pk, tgt_pk)` without passing `rel_type = row.get(\"rel_type\")`, causing `active_edge_keys` in one-click general inquiries to serialize with `-\u003eRELATED_TO-\u003e` instead of the authentic relationship type (`-\u003eENACTED_AS-\u003e`, `-\u003eMODIFIES_CODE-\u003e`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sufficiency \u0026 Scan Certification\n\nThe codebase dependency cone is exhaustively enumerated, all external/API schemas are grounded in observed empirical evidence saved in `assets/20261013T194318-162-mbmi/`, and this scan is certified **`{sufficient}`** under [LANGUAGE.md](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/LANGUAGE.md).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Handoff Manifest Affirmation\n\n[handoff/20261013T194318-162-mbmi/plan-scan-1.txt](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T194318-162-mbmi/handoff/20261013T194318-162-mbmi/plan-scan-1.txt) was atomically overwritten with exclusively the 32 repository-relative filepaths of qualified codebase components, the authored scan report, and the saved ground-truth payload files.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Coding Gate Affirmation\n\n*DO NOT CODE YET: Implementation coding gate remains locked. Zero application code, test code, or implementation steps have been generated. Coding waits on an empty frontier and explicit operator authorization.*\n\n\u003cpromise\u003eCOMPLETE\u003c/promise\u003e\n","duration_seconds":482.090471,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":193818,"output_tokens":39645,"thinking_tokens":12122,"cache_read_tokens":2063273,"total_tokens":233463}}}
